      "verdict": "partial",
      "gap": "The existence proof (annex lines 23-40) applies Radon-Nikodym on (Omega, G) with reference measure P restricted to G, so the densities satisfy nu_pm(A) = integral over A of Z_pm against P|_G. It then writes the integral of Z over A against P as nu_+(A) - nu_-(A) and asserts integrability with integrals EX^+ and EX^-; this needs the identity, with equal integrability status, between integrals of G-measurable nonnegative functions against P|_G and against P. The identity is not proved in the annex and is not stated anywhere on the route (it is supplied only in the off-route chapter conditioning-independence-and-information-w02c-p15-007.tex). Supply the step.",
